.TH SDL_memset 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_memset \- Initialize all bytes of buffer of memory to a specific value.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_stdinc.h>
.PP
.BI "void * SDL_memset(void *dst, int c, size_t len);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
This function will set
.BR len
bytes, pointed to by
.BR dst ,
to the value specified in
.BR c \[char46]
.PP
Despite
.BR c
being an
.BR int
instead of a
.BR char ,
this only operates on bytes;
.BR c
must be a value between 0 and 255, inclusive\[char46]

.SH FUNCTION PARAMETERS
.TP
.I dst
the destination memory region\[char46] Must not be NULL\[char46]
.TP
.I c
the byte value to set\[char46]
.TP
.I len
the length, in bytes, to set in
.BR dst \[char46]

.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns
.BR dst \[char46]

.SH THREAD SAFETY
It is safe to call this function from any thread\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This function is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

